018,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Information Services Group, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as an artificial intelligence (AI) centered technology research and advisory company in the Americas, Europe, and the Asia Pacific. It offers digital transformation services, including sourcing advisory and cloud and data analytics; managed governance and risk; network and software advisory; technology strategy and operations design; change management; and market intelligence. The company also provides ISG Digital, a client solution platform focused on developing technology, transformation, sourcing, and digital solutions; and ISG Enterprise, a client solution platform that helps clients manage change and optimize operations in such areas as information technology, finance, human resources, and training. In addition, it offers ISG Research, which provides market analyses, provider evaluations, and data-driven insights; ISG Network and Software Advisory portfolio; and ISG GovernX, ISG Inform, and ISG Tango software platforms, as well as ISG iFlex, a delivery model for deployment of resources. The company serves private sector clients operating in the manufacturing, banking and financial services, insurance, health sciences, energy and utilities, and consumer services industries; and public sector clients, including state and local governments, airport and transit authorities, and national and provincial government units. Information Services Group, Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is based in Stamford, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael P. Connors | Chairman & CEO | Age 70 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $163K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers. Each employee generates $17K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 16\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Information Services Group, Inc is a micro-cap technology business with a $294M market cap on $245M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +2.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $25M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.11\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 4.4\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 28% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3111931119311189},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (42% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 34% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 25% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"FutureBit brings home Bitcoin mining to Micro Center with Apollo III","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/futurebit-brings-home-bitcoin-mining-to-micro-center-with-apollo-iii-302937320.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794495000.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Branford Castle Acquires Floratine Products Group, Marking First Platform Investment in Fund III","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/branford-castle-acquires-floratine-products-group-marking-first-platform-investment-in-fund-iii-302937191.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794492000.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{